course: dictionary
lesson: 8960
title: Simplex: one part, one way
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Simplex is a long word, but its root is simple. A simplex thing is made of one part, not several parts joined together. When you meet a new word, ask: does this word look like a word I already know?
explain: «Cold sores are caused by a herpes simplex virus that stays in the body and can come back when you're ill or in the sun.» Here simplex is part of a name. The clues are that it is a virus and that it causes cold sores. If you swap in simple, «a herpes simple virus», it does not sound right, so simplex is a name here, not a description.
explain: In communication, a simplex link sends messages in only one direction, like a radio broadcast. A duplex link goes both ways. In maths, a simplex is the simplest shape in any number of dimensions. The meaning changes with the subject, so the subject is a clue too.
fact: Simplex means simple, made of one part, and not compound.
fact: A simplex link sends messages in only one direction, like a radio broadcast.
fact: Duplex is the opposite: it sends messages both ways.
fact: In maths, a simplex is the simplest shape: a point, a line segment, a triangle or a tetrahedron, depending on the number of dimensions.
fact: In «herpes simplex», simplex is the name of the virus that causes cold sores.
exercise: «Cold sores are caused by a herpes simplex virus that stays in the body.» In this sentence, what does simplex name? | A type of sunny holiday | *The virus that causes cold sores | A cold, wet day | A kind of doctor
exercise: In maths, which shape is a simplex in 2 dimensions? | A square | A circle | A cube | *A triangle
exercise: A simplex radio link sends messages how? | *Only one way, like a radio broadcast | Backwards and forwards in turn | Only when it is raining | Both ways at once
test: Simplex means which of these? | Made of many parts joined together | *Made of one part, simple | Very loud | Made of gold
test: Which link goes both ways, the opposite of simplex? | Simplex, which goes one way | *Duplex, which goes both ways | A tetrahedron | A cold sore
exam: In maths, what is a tetrahedron? | A flat circle with no corners | A 2-dimensional shape with four sides | *A 3-dimensional simplex, a triangle-based pyramid | A line with no ends
